  taDoc @[1] {
   name="ChangeLog";
   desc=;
   web_doc=0;
   wiki=;
   url="local";
   full_url="local";
   text_size=1;
   text="<html>
<head>ChangeLog</head>
<body>
<h1>ChangeLog</h1>
<ul>


<li>Sat Feb 10 21:40:05 2018 version: 0.1.66 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 415473 set a lot of relative layer positioning -- good layout for final fig.



<li>Fri Nov 17 00:15:48 2017 version: 0.1.65 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 415171 ACTUALLY turn monitors back on..



<li>Fri Nov 17 00:13:19 2017 version: 0.1.64 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 415170 turned ungp monitors back on



<li>Thu Nov 16 11:35:24 2017 version: 0.1.63 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 415166 monitor fixes from new error checking on monitors -- need to replace the ungp_data with new ungp path -- will do that tonight -- Tom if you have a more updated version of pvlv then perhaps you can merge these changes -- only changes were to monitor (and I switched the seq to pos acq for my basic test)



<li>Sun Jul  9 14:26:48 2017 version: 0.1.62 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414869 Update to data saving programs, now saves all crucial params for negative valence. Cond inhib behavior changed, will need to re-parameterize for fMRI.



<li>Fri May 26 21:42:07 2017 version: 0.1.61 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414792 commit pain expt changes again, just in case, had to do an emergent reconfigure for cluster run



<li>Fri May 26 19:19:00 2017 version: 0.1.60 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414791 add pain_exp config for loading pain expt data



<li>Sat Apr 15 14:21:14 2017 version: 0.1.59 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414696 fixes to add all neg_acq tests to the neg_acq_ext sequence in the TestSpec; param sets for VSMatrix negative valence learning rates



<li>Sat Apr 15 02:33:32 2017 version: 0.1.58 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414692 Many changes, both to infrastructure and params:
* updated MasterStartup, now detects if seq_params = automated_testing to determine whether to run that, shortened param name in cluster run etc.
* moved several param groups to PVLVStableMaster to make active set of params smaller.
* added _cont versions of pos_acq, new seq that does acq after ext -- I find this to be a good test of robustness of overall setup.
* param changes (all in PVLVRandy) -- archived Tom's prior active params before all this for reference.
:* slowed learning rates down dramatically across board -- idea is to be able to actually see the initial acquisition happening instead of that being over in first epoch or two.  increased cel g_bar.l leak to .8 to also slow that down a bit.
:* shrunk BLA back to 7x7 instead of 10x10 -- seems sufficient and runs a lot faster.
:* decreased inhib.fb_tau down to 3 -- didn't need to be that high
:* increased inhib.fb to 1 instead of .5 -- more fb = more direct competition -- don't need the redundant lateral inhib weights anymore I think (set abs = 0, should turn off prjn if ok)
:* potentially KEY factor: turned ON projection from context into BLA Pos D1 -- per anatomy these are *acq* guys and should get \"context\" inputs -- maybe key for allowing cond inhib to separate AX better -- didn't change context setting but that could also be experimented with -- but CI seems to be separating A and X fine and overall doing great -- ran it to 100 and is fully stable -- changed back to 25 to speed things up.
:* Ach is off for now -- haven't expt'd with turning that back on at all
:* cleaned up various specs that had overrides that weren't doing anything -- in general would be really good once this stabilizes to go back over and do \"compare with children\" and really push on making everything consistent -- esp for updating the wizard.




<li>Fri Apr 14 02:24:13 2017 version: 0.1.57 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414690 updated to latest working BFCS units -- fixed b50/b100 configs



<li>Fri Apr 14 01:59:19 2017 version: 0.1.56 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414689 * updated to BFCS ACh dynamics, modulating BLA -- turned decay to 0 on those weights -- but we don't have a good delta signal directly from either CEl or VSPatch.. maybe just take straight da for now??  but that has CS \"confound\" -- seems like it is US specific..
* misc fixes in project: changed basic PosAcq to PosAcq_B50 to indicate 50% reinforcement of B, and added B100 case (for direct comparison) -- B50 partial reinf should sustain more ACh than B100.  also added TRIAL_NAME stepping in MasterRun -- added those controls to ControlPanel.



<li>Wed Mar 29 15:13:34 2017 version: 0.1.55 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414650 fixes to cond_exp config, added load_exp variable to param set that is off in all other configs, but enabled for cond exp to allow data loading and saving from text files. 



<li>Thu Mar 30 01:05:55 2017 version: 0.1.54 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414649 * updated to latest ParamSet code
* added PVLV params group, set in MasterTrain, based on PVLV_03_20_17 set of params
* fixed issues in MasterStartup
* MasterTrainSeq now auto-detects null_step and stops at that point -- removed n_seq_steps from SeqParams.
* MasterTrain now updates its run_params to always be the current sequence step, if running a sequence, so that may be less confusing, and easier to just re-run that step if desired.
* All ready for Jessica to take over now -- definitely update to latest emergent code first!



<li>Fri Mar 24 14:21:18 2017 version: 0.1.53 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414642 Add SeqParams for all major configs to make it more convenient to run aba renewal, negative blocking, unblocking, summation test, overexpectation and magnitude change configs, etc. if running aba rewewal, set misc_params to ContextChange. 



<li>Sat Mar 25 02:30:21 2017 version: 0.1.52 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414641 updated cel project -- I'm handing off and heading to bed!



<li>Fri Mar 24 13:00:32 2017 version: 0.1.51 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414637 fix to saved_value paths in SeqParams -- will also fix this in the code soon



<li>Fri Mar 24 01:36:47 2017 version: 0.1.50 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414633 converted over to the new param-set based configuration -- seems to be working overall for the interactive runs. need to go over the testing config stuff -- seems like there is a ton of custom code there -- would be much better if this can all be much simpler and more automatic, based directly on the seq params cases. hopefully we can discuss in lab meeting.



<li>Wed Mar 22 19:18:25 2017 version: 0.1.49 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414631 minor fixes to cluster_run programs for cond_exp config



<li>Thu Mar  9 21:03:41 2017 version: 0.1.48 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel2.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414608 data saving and cond_exp config added to load experiment data. will do further testing with ClusterRun later.



<li>Tue Jan 10 17:00:06 2017 version: 0.1.47 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414517 from lab: now working for partial 50/50 and extinction!



<li>Tue Jan 10 12:42:31 2017 version: 0.1.46 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414516 higher cel leak, pptg gain



<li>Tue Jan 10 03:12:18 2017 version: 0.1.45 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414514 increase cel g_bar.l leak to .6 -- much more stable -- could potentially go higher on this.



<li>Tue Jan 10 02:55:48 2017 version: 0.1.44 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414513 blocking working..



<li>Tue Jan 10 02:49:01 2017 version: 0.1.43 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414512 cond inhib all working



<li>Tue Jan 10 01:02:40 2017 version: 0.1.42 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414509 finally, solid, sensible acq / ext / acq dynamics with sensible params, etc.



<li>Tue Jan 10 00:26:25 2017 version: 0.1.41 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414508 current best checkpoint -- just need to explore a few more params but don't want to lose these!



<li>Mon Jan  9 15:44:18 2017 version: 0.1.40 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414507 further exploration -- need differentiation in BLA learning..



<li>Mon Jan  9 14:04:37 2017 version: 0.1.39 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414506 * can step to any arbitrary trial (uses contains -- wildcard-ish)
* getting bizzare activation explosion and weight decrease on first omit_t2 trial.. need to debug but leaving soon..



<li>Mon Jan  9 03:10:37 2017 version: 0.1.38 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414505 * new BLA decay function and much improved behavior overall
* new epoch-based trial type graph for looking at trends over time
* improved graphing setup with auto-comparison graphs and properly labeled trial monitor items by US type and BLA for US etc.




<li>Sun Jan  8 03:07:46 2017 version: 0.1.37 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414503 many fixes:
* permuted order of events
* mean in graphing
* group-based org of BLA -- VS really needs this -- was getting weird mass effects from colleteral activations
* good overall acq, ext, acq behavior -- BLA needs more novelty though -- had that at one point..
* CeM gets both CEl D1 and D2




<li>Sat Jan  7 02:44:29 2017 version: 0.1.36 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414501 do acq after ext -- revealing -- more notes on params



<li>Sat Jan  7 02:35:28 2017 version: 0.1.35 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414500 much more sensible -- still not getting sig BLA decay effects -- may need a delayed dynamic of some sort??



<li>Fri Jan  6 02:57:02 2017 version: 0.1.34 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414496 param exploration results -- good overall params for basic pos_acq_extinct with various notes



<li>Thu Jan  5 03:41:44 2017 version: 0.1.33 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414493 * new graph options (labels, flip)
* experiments with decay params



<li>Thu Jan  5 00:41:08 2017 version: 0.1.32 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414492 * fix dyn enum pointers in bvPVLVEnv program
* remove unused programs
* load_weights config flag auto-uses prior weights in config sequences



<li>Mon Jan  2 03:13:51 2017 version: 0.1.31 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414486 support for sequences of configs using network weight-save objects to carry weights across configs.  and cleanup of config table.  extinction mostly working.



<li>Sat Dec 31 03:25:26 2016 version: 0.1.30 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414485 unit-group based BLA, new scale-based random weights that allow randomness with low initial weight values -- good qualitative pos_acq behavior



<li>Fri Dec 30 02:36:08 2016 version: 0.1.29 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414484 fully cortex-like BLA -- VS can learn to interpret -- need to try some different paradigms to explore BLA contributions -- basic acq works but is somewhat noisy.



<li>Thu Dec 29 02:20:24 2016 version: 0.1.28 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414481 * renamed BA->CEl
* replaced RTOut code etc with TrialAnalysis program based on TickAnalysis -- automatically updates group spec based on trial log data so you only have to change in one place and everything else is automatic. also other cleanup of monitoring etc code.



<li>Mon Dec 26 01:49:05 2016 version: 0.1.27 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414478 actually lat amyg should have higher act to allow more graded learning.. 

more acq -> ext inhib worked -- get more of a 50/50 for acq/ext on 50/50 conditioning probability..



<li>Tue Dec  6 22:49:16 2016 version: 0.1.26 user: jmollick file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414441 fixed RealTimeOutput graph, looks back to normal. VTA UserData logging fixed, can be turned on or off with the alpha_trial_monitor_vta flag on ControlPanel.



<li>Tue Dec  6 15:13:19 2016 version: 0.1.25 user: jmollick file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414439 fixed vta_list UserData issues so project can open again



<li>Mon Dec  5 19:01:13 2016 version: 0.1.24 user: jmollick file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414436 new function monitor_vta in alpha_trial_monitor to allow monitoring vta user data values. can be switched off with the alpha_trial_monitor_monitor_vta on the ControlPanel.



<li>Mon Oct 17 20:06:00 2016 version: 0.1.23 user: jmollick file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414303 Expanded USTime_In layer to allow W and Z stimuli to have both reward and punishment associations, adjusted avg_act init of USTime_In to .003, added pos_neg config for testing stimuli with both reward and punishment associations



<li>Wed Oct 12 14:28:09 2016 version: 0.1.22 user: anantanair file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414280 Renamed time and stimulus local vars to time_val and stimulus_val to avoid conflict 



<li>Tue Oct  4 23:07:30 2016 version: 0.1.21 user: jmollick file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414253 Put ContextModel on Control Panel



<li>Tue Oct  4 17:45:31 2016 version: 0.1.20 user: jmollick file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414252 Update VSMatrixPosD1Units raw thr rel and raw thr abs to 0.01



<li>Tue Oct  4 16:46:00 2016 version: 0.1.19 user: jmollick file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414250 Fixes to the VSMatrixPosD2 connection from VSMatrixPosD2, increase the wt_scale_abs strength of the Deep_Mod_Fm_VSMatrixPosD1 to 1. Fixes the deep_mod_net issues with VSMatrixPosD2.



<li>Fri Sep 16 00:01:56 2016 version: 0.1.18 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414194 * new msn_deriv flag must be OFF fro VSMatrixCons, because of the deep_lrn always being 1, and thus 1-1 = 0 and no learning occurs..
* all vsmatrixconspecs inherit the \"trace\" field from parent.
* also updated list of variables displayed in network



<li>Tue Sep  6 17:02:44 2016 version: 0.1.17 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414168 all authors now added..



<li>Mon Aug 22 10:29:33 2016 version: 0.1.16 user: thazy file_name: <code>bvPVLV.proj</code> <br>
Published on wiki: CCN page: bvPVLV with description: bi-valent Primary Value Learned Value model of the phasic dopamine signaling system tags: PVLV, Leabra, flex author: Thomas Hazy, Jessica Mollick, Ananta Nair, Kai Krueger email: thazy@colorado.edu, jmollick@gmail.com, ananta.nair@colorado.edu, kai.krueger@colorado.edu version: 0.1.15 pub_cite: 
</ul>
</body>
</html>
";
   html_text="<html>
<head>ChangeLog</head>
<body>
<h1>ChangeLog</h1>
<ul>
<P>
<P>
<li>Sat Feb 10 21:40:05 2018 version: 0.1.66 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 415473 set a lot of relative layer positioning -- good layout for final fig.
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri Nov 17 00:15:48 2017 version: 0.1.65 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 415171 ACTUALLY turn monitors back on..
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri Nov 17 00:13:19 2017 version: 0.1.64 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 415170 turned ungp monitors back on
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Thu Nov 16 11:35:24 2017 version: 0.1.63 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 415166 monitor fixes from new error checking on monitors -- need to replace the ungp_data with new ungp path -- will do that tonight -- Tom if you have a more updated version of pvlv then perhaps you can merge these changes -- only changes were to monitor (and I switched the seq to pos acq for my basic test)
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Sun Jul  9 14:26:48 2017 version: 0.1.62 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414869 Update to data saving programs, now saves all crucial params for negative valence. Cond inhib behavior changed, will need to re-parameterize for fMRI.
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri May 26 21:42:07 2017 version: 0.1.61 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414792 commit pain expt changes again, just in case, had to do an emergent reconfigure for cluster run
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri May 26 19:19:00 2017 version: 0.1.60 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414791 add pain_exp config for loading pain expt data
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Sat Apr 15 14:21:14 2017 version: 0.1.59 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414696 fixes to add all neg_acq tests to the neg_acq_ext sequence in the TestSpec; param sets for VSMatrix negative valence learning rates
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Sat Apr 15 02:33:32 2017 version: 0.1.58 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414692 Many changes, both to infrastructure and params:
<ul><li> updated MasterStartup, now detects if seq_params = automated_testing to determine whether to run that, shortened param name in cluster run etc.
<li> moved several param groups to PVLVStableMaster to make active set of params smaller.
<li> added _cont versions of pos_acq, new seq that does acq after ext -- I find this to be a good test of robustness of overall setup.
<li> param changes (all in PVLVRandy) -- archived Tom's prior active params before all this for reference.
<ul><li> slowed learning rates down dramatically across board -- idea is to be able to actually see the initial acquisition happening instead of that being over in first epoch or two.  increased cel g_bar.l leak to .8 to also slow that down a bit.
<li> shrunk BLA back to 7x7 instead of 10x10 -- seems sufficient and runs a lot faster.
<li> decreased inhib.fb_tau down to 3 -- didn't need to be that high
<li> increased inhib.fb to 1 instead of .5 -- more fb = more direct competition -- don't need the redundant lateral inhib weights anymore I think (set abs = 0, should turn off prjn if ok)
<li> potentially KEY factor: turned ON projection from context into BLA Pos D1 -- per anatomy these are *acq* guys and should get \"context\" inputs -- maybe key for allowing cond inhib to separate AX better -- didn't change context setting but that could also be experimented with -- but CI seems to be separating A and X fine and overall doing great -- ran it to 100 and is fully stable -- changed back to 25 to speed things up.
<li> Ach is off for now -- haven't expt'd with turning that back on at all
<li> cleaned up various specs that had overrides that weren't doing anything -- in general would be really good once this stabilizes to go back over and do \"compare with children\" and really push on making everything consistent -- esp for updating the wizard.
</ul></ul>
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri Apr 14 02:24:13 2017 version: 0.1.57 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414690 updated to latest working BFCS units -- fixed b50/b100 configs
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri Apr 14 01:59:19 2017 version: 0.1.56 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414689 * updated to BFCS ACh dynamics, modulating BLA -- turned decay to 0 on those weights -- but we don't have a good delta signal directly from either CEl or VSPatch.. maybe just take straight da for now??  but that has CS \"confound\" -- seems like it is US specific..
<ul><li> misc fixes in project: changed basic PosAcq to PosAcq_B50 to indicate 50% reinforcement of B, and added B100 case (for direct comparison) -- B50 partial reinf should sustain more ACh than B100.  also added TRIAL_NAME stepping in MasterRun -- added those controls to ControlPanel.
</ul>
<P>
<P>
<li>Wed Mar 29 15:13:34 2017 version: 0.1.55 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414650 fixes to cond_exp config, added load_exp variable to param set that is off in all other configs, but enabled for cond exp to allow data loading and saving from text files. 
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Thu Mar 30 01:05:55 2017 version: 0.1.54 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414649 * updated to latest ParamSet code
<ul><li> added PVLV params group, set in MasterTrain, based on PVLV_03_20_17 set of params
<li> fixed issues in MasterStartup
<li> MasterTrainSeq now auto-detects null_step and stops at that point -- removed n_seq_steps from SeqParams.
<li> MasterTrain now updates its run_params to always be the current sequence step, if running a sequence, so that may be less confusing, and easier to just re-run that step if desired.
<li> All ready for Jessica to take over now -- definitely update to latest emergent code first!
</ul>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri Mar 24 14:21:18 2017 version: 0.1.53 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414642 Add SeqParams for all major configs to make it more convenient to run aba renewal, negative blocking, unblocking, summation test, overexpectation and magnitude change configs, etc. if running aba rewewal, set misc_params to ContextChange. 
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Sat Mar 25 02:30:21 2017 version: 0.1.52 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414641 updated cel project -- I'm handing off and heading to bed!
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri Mar 24 13:00:32 2017 version: 0.1.51 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414637 fix to saved_value paths in SeqParams -- will also fix this in the code soon
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Fri Mar 24 01:36:47 2017 version: 0.1.50 user: oreilly file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414633 converted over to the new param-set based configuration -- seems to be working overall for the interactive runs. need to go over the testing config stuff -- seems like there is a ton of custom code there -- would be much better if this can all be much simpler and more automatic, based directly on the seq params cases. hopefully we can discuss in lab meeting.
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Wed Mar 22 19:18:25 2017 version: 0.1.49 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414631 minor fixes to cluster_run programs for cond_exp config
<P>
<P>
<P>
<li>Thu Mar  9 21:03:41 2017 version: 0.1.48 user: ccnlab file_name: <code>bvPVLV_cel2.proj</code> <br>
svn rev: 414608 data saving and cond_exp config added to load experiment data. will do further testing with ClusterRun later.
<P>
